            "size": 5002,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "[{\"result\":{\"data\":{\"designGuide\":\"# Brand Design Guide: OLIPOP\\n\\nThis document serves as the primary visual reference for all ad creative designers. OLIPOP’s brand identity is a \\\"Retro-Modern\\\" aesthetic that blends vintage, nostalgic typography with clean, vibrant, and health-conscious modern design.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Typography\\nOLIPOP uses a distinct combination of a chunky, vintage serif for personality and a clean, geometric sans-serif for legibility.\\n\\n### **Primary Headline Font: WindsorEF**\\n*   **Description:** A heavy, nostalgic serif font with a \\\"700s/70s feel.\\\" It features rounded terminals and high contrast between thick and thin strokes. It feels friendly, organic, and premium.\\n*   **Weights:** Bold (700) and UltraHeavy (900).\\n*   **Usage:** Used for main headlines, \\\"Why\\\" statements, and big punchy callouts.\\n*   **Designer Tip:** When using this, keep tracking (letter spacing) tight to maintain that \\\"chunky\\\" vintage look.\\n\\n### **Secondary/Body Font: Ano**\\n*   **Description:** A modern, geometric sans-serif. It is very clean, open, and highly legible. It balances the \\\"busy-ness\\\" of the Windsor font.\\n*   **Weights:** Regular, Bold, and Black (900).\\n*   **Usage:** Body copy, buttons, product descriptions, and navigation elements.\\n*   **Designer Tip:** Use the \\\"Black\\\" weight for sub-headlines to create a clear hierarchy.\\n\\n### **System Fallbacks**\\n*   If the above are unavailable, use: **Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Color Palette\\nThe OLIPOP palette is anchored in deep, \\\"Hunter\\\" greens balanced by bright, sunny yellows and clean whites.\\n\\n| Color Name | Hex Code | Human Description |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Hunter Green** | `#14433D` | A deep, sophisticated forest green. The primary anchor color for the brand. |\\n| **Deep Forest** | `#034638` | A slightly darker, cooler green used for high-contrast text on bright backgrounds. |\\n| **Citron Yellow** | `#FFFF7D` | A soft, buttery \\\"pale sun\\\" yellow. Used for primary buttons and accents. |\\n| **Electric Lime** | `#E2EB28` | A vibrant, neon-leaning yellow-green. Used for hover states and grabbing attention. |\\n| **Charcoal** | `#3A3A3A` | A soft off-black used for primary text to avoid the harshness of pure black. |\\n| **Off-White** | `#FFF7E5` | A warm, creamy \\\"eggshell\\\" white used for backgrounds to enhance the vintage feel. |\\n| **Sale Red** | `#FA4545` | A bright, punchy \\\"pop\\\" red used exclusively for urgency or discount callouts. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Key Visual Motifs\\n\\n### **The \\\"Wave\\\" Separator**\\nOLIPOP frequently uses a **Wave/Curve** motif to separate sections rather than straight lines.\\n*   **Style:** Gentle, organic curves.\\n*   **Usage:** Use these to transition between background colors (e.g., a Hunter Green wave flowing into a White background). It mimics the liquid nature of the product.\\n\\n### **Button Styles**\\n*   **Shape:** \\\"Pill\\\" style (fully rounded corners/large border-radius).\\n*   **Standard CTA:** Citron Yellow (`#FFFF7D`) background with Deep Forest (`#034638`) text.\\n*   **Primary Bold CTA:** Hunter Green (`#14433D`) background with White text.\\n*   **Interactive feel:** Buttons should feel \\\"clickable\\\" and friendly, never sharp-edged.\\n\\n### **Icons & Symbols**\\n*   **Checkmarks:** Simple, minimalist check symbols are used for benefit callouts (e.g., \\\"9g Fiber,\\\" \\\"Low Sugar\\\").\\n*   **Spinning Elements:** The brand uses a simple 360-degree spin animation for loading or subtle attention-grabbing elements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Hierarchy & Spacing\\n*   **Desktop Headlines:** Large and bold (approx 35px–48px).\\n*   **Mobile Headlines:** Scaled down but still dominant (approx 32px).\\n*   **Body Text:** Clean and airy. Standard body size is roughly 15px–16px with a line height of 1.4 to 1.5.\\n*   **White Space:** Don't crowd the product. Let the vintage typography and the colorful cans have room to \\\"breathe.\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Notes for Designers\\n*   **Context is Key:** This guide provides the visual \\\"ingredients.\\\" You do not need to use every element in every ad. \\n*   **The Mascot/Graphic Rule:** If a specific mascot, fruit illustration, or wave graphic is mentioned in the brand assets, only use it if it aligns with the specific campaign. For example, use fruit illustrations for flavor-specific ads, but keep it minimal for brand-wide \\\"Why Olipop\\\" ads.\\n*   **Vintage vs. Modern:** Always aim for the \\\"sweet spot\\\" between 1970s soda nostalgia and 2024 health-tech. If the design feels too \\\"old,\\\" simplify the background. If it feels too \\\"modern/techy,\\\" swap a headline to WindsorEF.\\n*   **Hierarchy:** The product (the can) and the headline should always be the stars. Use the Hunter Green and Citron Yellow to guide the eye to the CTA.\\n\\n---\\n*This guide is for internal creative use. Please refer to these hex codes and font descriptions for all digital and print ad placements.*\",\"sourceJobId\":\"6a54a7d9-53f7-4070-92e4-22ea3e97270b\",\"referenceAdDesignImages\":[]}}}]"
          },
