image is the official brand logo. Add it once, subtly, in clean negative space; keep it exact, legible, and uncropped.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"source\":\"campaign-creatives\",\"language\":\"English\",\"lastError\":null,\"imageModel\":\"openai/gpt-image-2:100\",\"hasNSFWRisk\":false,\"imagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Based on the Side-by-Side Comparison (SBSC) framework, this static 1:1 graphic directly compares OLIPOP Classic Grape to traditional grape soda to prove it is the ultimate health upgrade. The layout is a clean, split-screen design. The left half has a charcoal background showing a generic, dusty-looking purple soda can dripping with artificial syrup next to a harsh red warning label reading \\\"39g Sugar\\\". The right half features a warm, welcoming off-white background highlighting the matte, pastel lavender-lilac OLIPOP Classic Grape can sitting on a clean surface with a small checkmark list pointing to \\\"5g Sugar\\\" and \\\"9g Fiber\\\". The visual hero is the contrast between the toxic old choice and the clean, premium new upgrade. The on-image headline is \\\"Same nostalgic taste, 85% less sugar.\\\" in the bold, vintage WindsorEF typeface 