rand, ensure the lighting is natural and airy, use the brand's secondary Ano typeface for the benefit text, and maintain the retro-modern aesthetic with generous whitespace around the product.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Based on the Problem-Agitate-Solve (PAS) framework, this static 1:1 ad targets consumers who love soda but hate the bloating and digestive discomfort that traditional sugary drinks cause. The layout is an elegant, in-context lifestyle photograph set in a bright, modern kitchen during a sunny morning. The visual hero is the outcome: a cold, condensation-ringed pastel lavender OLIPOP Classic Grape can next to a beautiful tall glass filled with ice, dark purple grape soda, and a fresh lime wedge, symbolizing a clean, refreshing, and gut-friendly afternoon treat. Text is kept minimal, under 20% of the frame. The on-image headline reads \\\"The soda that loves your gut.\\\" set in WindsorEF in Deep Forest. A simple checkmark icon points out \\\"9g Plant Fiber\\\" and \\\"Prebiotics\\\". The single clear call to action is a pill-shaped Hunter Green button reading \\\"See The Difference\\\". To keep this ad on-brand, ensure the lighting is natural and airy, use the brand's secondary Ano typeface for the benefit text, and maintain the retro-modern aesthetic with generous whitespace around the product.\\n\\nProduct appearance: This 12 fl oz (355 mL) aluminum beverage can features a cylindrical silhouette with a silver metallic top rim, a standard silver pull tab, and a silver bottom rim. The primary version of the can has a matte, pastel lavender-lilac finish, adorned on the front with the brand name OLIPOP arched across the upper third in bold, deep violet-purple uppercase letters. Centered below the brand name is a graphic of a stylized grape cluster composed of thirteen solid violet-purple circles, crowned by a single curved, dark forest-green leaf and stem pointing left. Beneath this graphic, the flavor name Classic Grape is written in a