eckmark list pointing to \\\"5g Sugar\\\" and \\\"9g Fiber\\\". The visual hero is the contrast between the toxic old choice and the clean, premium new upgrade. The on-image headline is \\\"Same nostalgic taste, 85% less sugar.\\\" in the bold, vintage WindsorEF typeface in Hunter Green, keeping text under 20% of the image. The single call to action is a pill-shaped Citron Yellow button that reads \\\"Compare Now\\\". To keep this ad on-brand, use WindsorEF for the main headline, use Hunter Green for the right-side elements, ensure the off-white background feels creamy and organic, and avoid pure black in favor of Charcoal for secondary text.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Based on the Side-by-Side Comparison (SBSC) framework, this static 1:1 graphic directly compares OLIPOP Classic Grape to traditional grape soda to prove it is the ultimate health upgrade. The layout is a clean, split-screen design. The left half has a charcoal background showing a generic, dusty-looking purple soda can dripping with artificial syrup next to a harsh red warning label reading \\\"39g Sugar\\\". The right half features a warm, welcoming off-white background highlighting the matte, pastel lavender-lilac OLIPOP Classic Grape can sitting on a clean surface with a small checkmark list pointing to \\\"5g Sugar\\\" and \\\"9g Fiber\\\". The visual hero is the contrast between the toxic old choice and the clean, premium new upgrade. The on-image headline is \\\"Same nostalgic taste, 85% less sugar.\\\" in the bold, vintage WindsorEF typeface in Hunter Green, keeping text under 20% of the image. The single call to action is a pill-shaped Citron Yellow button that reads \\\"Compare Now\\\". To keep this ad on-brand, use WindsorEF for the main headline, use Hunter Green for the right-side elements, ensure the off-white background feels creamy and organic, and avoid pure black in favor of Charcoal for secondary text.\\n\\nProduct appearance: This 12 fl oz (355 mL) aluminum beverag