24c-33e5-4e33-8da0-d728f3743739\",\"triggerRunId\":null,\"changeType\":\"initial\",\"instructions\":null,\"finalImagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Based on the Problem-Agitate-Solve (PAS) framework, this static 1:1 ad targets consumers who love soda but hate the bloating and digestive discomfort that traditional sugary drinks cause. The layout is an elegant, in-context lifestyle photograph set in a bright, modern kitchen during a sunny morning. The visual hero is the outcome: a cold, condensation-ringed pastel lavender OLIPOP Classic Grape can next to a beautiful tall glass filled with ice, dark purple grape soda, and a fresh lime wedge, symbolizing a clean, refreshing, and gut-friendly afternoon treat. Text is kept minimal, under 20% of the frame. The on-image headline reads \\\"The soda that loves your gut.\\\" set in WindsorEF in Deep Forest. A simple checkmark icon points out \\\"9g Plant Fiber\\\" and \\\"Prebiotics\\\". The single clear call to action is a pill-shaped Hunter Green button reading \\\"See The Difference\\\". To keep this ad on-brand, ensure the lighting is natural and airy, use the brand's secondary Ano typeface for the benefit text, and maintain the retro-modern aesthetic with generous whitespace around the product.\\n\\nProduct appearance: This 12 fl oz (355 mL) aluminum beverage can features a cylindrical silhouette with a silver metallic top rim, a standard silver pull tab, and a silver bottom rim. The primary version of the can has a matte, pastel lavender-lilac finish, adorned on the front with the brand name OLIPOP arched across the upper third in bold, deep violet-purple uppercase letters. Centered below the brand name is a graphic of a stylized grape cluster composed of thirteen solid violet-purple circles, crowned by a single curved, dark forest-green leaf and stem pointing left. Beneath this graphic, the flavor name Classic Grape is written in a dark forest-green serif typeface across two lines. Further down, the tagline A New Kind of Soda is printed in a smaller violet-purple sans-serif font, with the volume 12 fl oz (355 mL) centered at the bottom. The upper shoulder of the can features the phrase Supports Digestive Health in small dark forest-green sans-serif text. Flanking the central graphics on the left are the words Prebiotics, Botanicals, and Plant Fiber, with Non GMO at the bottom left; the right side features a small circular Plant Powered Microbiome Approved seal and the callout 5g of sugar per can at the bottom right. A secondary version of the product is also visible, which reverses the colorway to feature a deep royal-purple can body with white lettering for the brand name, flavor, and side text, while the grape graphic is highlighted with lighter lavender tones.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nThe final attached image is the official brand logo. Add it once, subtly, in clean negative space; keep it exact, legible, and uncropped.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"status\":\"generating\",\"createdBy\":\"f5dfb377-dac7-46a6-aea3-a4e04cb45e54\",\"metadata\":{\"brief\":\"Based on the Problem-Agitate-Solve (PAS) framework, this static 1:1 ad targets consumers who love soda but hate the bloating and digestive discomfort that traditional sugary drinks cause. The layout is an elegant, in-context lifestyle photograph set in a bright, modern kitchen during a sunny morning. The visual hero is the outcome: a cold, condensation-ringed pastel lavender OLIPOP Classic Grape can next to a beautiful tall glass filled with ice, dark purple grape soda, and a fresh lime wedge, symbolizing a clean, refreshing, and gut-friendly afternoon treat. Text is kept minimal, under 20% of the frame. The on-image headline reads \\\"The soda that loves your gut.\\\" set in WindsorEF in Deep Forest. A simple checkmark icon points out \\\"9g Plant Fiber\\\" and \\\"Prebiotics\\\". The single clear call to action is a pill-shaped Hunter Green button reading \\\"See The Difference\\\". To keep this ad on-brand, ensure the lighting is natural and airy, use the brand's secondary Ano typeface for the benefit text, and maintain the retro-modern aesthetic with generous whitespace around the product.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Based on the Problem-Agitate-Solve (PAS) framework, this static 1:1 ad targets consumers who love soda but hate the bloating and digestive discomfort that traditional sugary drinks cause. The layout is an elegant, in-context lifestyle photograph set in a bright, modern kitchen during a sunny morning. The visual hero is the outcome: a cold, condensation-ringed pastel lavender OLIPOP Classic Grape can next to a beautiful tall glass filled with ice, dark