eep it exact, legible, and uncropped.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"source\":\"campaign-creatives\",\"language\":\"English\",\"lastError\":null,\"imageModel\":\"gpt-image-2\",\"hasNSFWRisk\":false,\"imagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Based on the Contrast and Choice (CC) framework, this static 1:1 ad targets routine diet soda drinkers by positioning OLIPOP as the premium, clean-label upgrade that eliminates chemical sweeteners. The layout is a bold, retro-modern studio shot divided by a gentle, organic Hunter Green wave separator. The bottom section is a deep, warm off-white, while the top section features the wave. The visual hero is the secondary version of the OLIPOP Classic Grape can, which features a deep royal-purple body with white lettering, standing proudly on a pedestal of real, fresh Concord grapes. This premium presentation emphasizes clean, plant-powered ingredients over synthetic diet alternatives. The on-image headline is \\\"Ditch diet chemicals. Upgrade your soda.\\\" in the ultra-heavy weight of the WindsorEF font in Hunter Green. The single call to action is a vibrant Citron Yellow pill-style button with Deep Forest text reading \\\"Try It Now\\\". T