tom section is a deep, warm off-white, while the top section features the wave. The visual hero is the secondary version of the OLIPOP Classic Grape can, which features a deep royal-purple body with white lettering, standing proudly on a pedestal of real, fresh Concord grapes. This premium presentation emphasizes clean, plant-powered ingredients over synthetic diet alternatives. The on-image headline is \\\"Ditch diet chemicals. Upgrade your soda.\\\" in the ultra-heavy weight of the WindsorEF font in Hunter Green. The single call to action is a vibrant Citron Yellow pill-style button with Deep Forest text reading \\\"Try It Now\\\". To keep this ad on-brand, use the signature wave motif to partition the graphic, ensure color hex codes match the Citron Yellow and Hunter Green brand palette, and keep the typography tightly tracked for that nostalgic, chunky look.\\n\\nProduct appearance: This 12 fl oz (355 mL) aluminum beverage can features a cylindrical silhouette with a silver metallic top rim, a standard silver pull tab, and a silver bottom rim. The primary version of the can has a matte, pastel lavender-lilac finish, adorned on the front with the brand name OLIPOP arched across the upper third in bold, deep violet-purple uppercase letters. Centered below the brand name is a graphic of a stylized grape cluster composed of thirteen solid violet-purple circles, crowned by a single curved, dark forest-green leaf and stem pointing left. Beneath this graphic, the flavor name Classic Grape is written in a dark forest-green serif typeface across two lines. Further down, the tagline A New Kind of Soda is printed in a smaller violet-purple sans-serif font, with the volume 12 fl oz (355 mL) centered at the bottom. The upper shoulder of the can features the phrase Supports Digestive Health in small dark forest-green sans-serif text. Flanking the central graphics on the left are the words Prebiotics, Botanicals, and Plant Fiber, with Non GMO at the bottom left; the right side